<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Continuation of Enrolment' }) %>
<%
  // Continuation of Enrolment — the 2027 campaign view (Nov 2026 → Apr 2027). Counts only, no names:
  // a viewer may open this page. Every figure states its method beside it.
  const shortName = (n) => (n||'').replace(/Futuro Childcare (and|&) Education\s*-?\s*/i,'').replace('Futuro ','').trim();
  const MN = ['Jan','Feb','Mar','Apr','May','Jun','Jul','Aug','Sep','Oct','Nov','Dec'];
  const mLong  = (mo) => MN[Number(mo.slice(5,7))-1] + ' ' + mo.slice(0,4);
  const mShort = (mo) => MN[Number(mo.slice(5,7))-1] + ' ' + mo.slice(2,4);
  const dLong  = (d) => d ? new Date(d+'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-AU',{day:'numeric',month:'short',year:'numeric'}) : '';
  const fmt  = (n) => Math.round(Number(n)||0).toLocaleString('en-AU');
  const sgn  = (n) => (Number(n)||0) > 0 ? '−' + fmt(n) : fmt(n);
  const TGT  = coe.target_pct;
  const tone = (p) => p >= TGT ? 'good' : (p >= TGT - 10 ? 'warn' : 'bad');
  const W    = (v, avail) => avail > 0 ? Math.max(0, Math.min(100, v / avail * 100)).toFixed(1) : '0';
  // Anchor month: February 2027, the first full month after the school-year transition.
  let ai = coe.months.findIndex((x) => x.month === '2027-02');
  if (ai < 0) ai = Math.min(3, coe.months.length - 1);
  const am = coe.months[ai], ga = coe.group.months[ai];
  const openMonth = (c) => c.opening_month ? MN[c.opening_month-1] + ' ' + c.opening_year : (c.opening_year || 'soon');
  // The measured half: null until the first nightly snapshot has run (services/snapshot.js runCoeSnapshot).
  const ms = coe.measured;
  const mi = ms ? ms.months.findIndex((x) => x.month === am.month) : -1;
  const mm = mi >= 0 ? ms.months[mi] : null;
  const mixBand = (o, d) => (o.mix.find((x) => x.days_per_week === d) || { children: 0, child_days: 0 });
%>

<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1>Continuation of Enrolment
      <% if (ms) { %><span class="badge">Measured continuing count as at <%= dLong(ms.snapshot_date) %></span>
      <% } else { %><span class="badge warn">First release — continuing count and booking mix follow</span><% } %>
    </h1>
    <p class="sub">The 2027 campaign view · <%= mLong(coe.window.first) %> – <%= mLong(coe.window.last) %> · child-days booked against child-days available, per centre · counts only, no child, family or staff names</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="border-left:3px solid var(--warn);">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Read these three limits before you read the numbers</h2>
  <ol class="coe-limits">
    <% if (mm) { %>
    <li><strong>The run rate assumes every family without a finish date continues, so it is a ceiling — the measured count beside it does not.</strong> Nobody has told us they are staying, so the run rate only counts who has not told us they are leaving. As at <%= dLong(ms.snapshot_date) %>, of the <%= fmt(mm.enrolled) %> children enrolled today, <strong><%= fmt(mm.continuing) %> hold bookings that reach <%= mLong(am.month) %></strong>, <%= fmt(mm.not_confirmed) %> have none that far out yet and <%= fmt(mm.leaving) %> have a finish date before it. Read the percentages in this section as the best case and the measured count below as what is actually booked.</li>
    <% } else { %>
    <li><strong>The run rate assumes every family without a finish date continues, so it is a ceiling.</strong> Nobody has told us they are staying — we have only counted who has not told us they are leaving. The measured per-child continuing count starts accumulating from the first nightly run (2:15am Sydney, or on demand with <code>npm run coe-snapshot</code>) and appears on this page from then on; until then treat every percentage as the best case.</li>
    <% } %>
    <li><strong>January reads high because leavers are still present until late January while starters are added from their start dates.</strong> The two groups overlap inside the month, so <%= mLong('2027-01') %> is the crossover, not a genuine peak. February is the first clean month.</li>
    <li><strong>Leaver days are estimated from each centre's average booking pattern, not each leaver's own days.</strong> The count of leavers is exact — it comes from finish dates set in OWNA — but the child-days they remove use the centre average (<%= coe.centres.map((c) => shortName(c.name) + ' ' + c.avg_days_per_child.toFixed(1)).join(', ') %> days per child per week). A centre losing mostly five-day families will lose more than shown; mostly two-day families, less.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="footnote" style="margin-bottom:0;">Built from the snapshot as at <%= dLong(coe.as_at) %>. Run-rate week <%= dLong(coe.run_week.from) %> – <%= dLong(coe.run_week.to) %> (the last complete Mon–Fri week, the same week for every centre). Pipeline starts counted from <%= dLong(coe.pipeline_from) %>. Operating days exclude weekends and NSW public holidays<%= coe.unknown_holiday_years.length ? ' (no gazetted list yet for ' + coe.unknown_holiday_years.join(', ') + ' — weekdays only)' : '' %>.</p>
</div>

<div class="grid kpis">
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= fmt(ga.available_days) %></div><div class="l">Child-days available in <%= mLong(am.month) %><span class="cap"><%= coe.group.places %> licensed places × <%= am.operating_days %> operating days</span></div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n <%= tone(ga.pct) + '-text' %>"><%= ga.pct %>%</div><div class="l">Projected filled · <%= fmt(ga.projected_days) %> days<span class="cap">run rate − leaver days + firm backfill · target <%= TGT %>% is a placeholder</span></div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n bad-text"><%= sgn(ga.leaver_days) %></div><div class="l">Child-days falling away<span class="cap"><%= ga.leavers_to_date %> children with a finish date set by <%= mLong(am.month) %>, at each centre's average booking pattern</span></div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n good-text">+<%= fmt(ga.firm_days) %></div><div class="l">Child-days of firm backfill<span class="cap"><%= ga.firm_children %> children at Offer Accepted or Pre-Offered, from their expected start date<%= ga.days_unknown ? ' · ' + ga.days_unknown + ' of them with no requested days recorded, valued at their centre average' : '' %></span></div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= ga.gap_days > 0 ? fmt(ga.gap_days) : '—' %></div><div class="l">Gap to the <%= TGT %>% placeholder target<span class="cap">child-days in <%= mLong(am.month) %><%= ga.gap_days > 0 && am.operating_days ? ' · about ' + Math.round(ga.gap_days / (am.operating_days / 5) / 3) + ' children at 3 days a week' : ' · the projection is at or above the placeholder' %></span></div></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;"><%= mLong(am.month) %>, the anchor month <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400;font-size:13px;">· each bar is that centre's available child-days</span></h2>
  <% coe.centres.forEach(function(c){ var x = c.months[ai]; var keep = Math.max(0, x.run_rate_days - x.leaver_days); %>
    <div class="coe-bar-row">
      <div class="coe-bar-name"><%= shortName(c.name) %><span><%= c.places %> places · <%= am.operating_days %> days · <%= fmt(x.available_days) %> days available</span></div>
      <div class="coe-track">
        <div class="coe-seg keep" style="width:<%= W(keep, x.available_days) %>%;" title="Run rate less leavers: <%= fmt(keep) %> days"></div>
        <div class="coe-seg firm" style="width:<%= W(x.firm_days, x.available_days) %>%;" title="Firm backfill: <%= fmt(x.firm_days) %> days"></div>
        <div class="coe-seg lost" style="width:<%= W(x.leaver_days, x.available_days) %>%;" title="Days falling away: <%= fmt(x.leaver_days) %> days"></div>
        <div class="coe-target" style="left:<%= TGT %>%;" title="Placeholder target <%= TGT %>%"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="coe-bar-val <%= tone(x.pct) + '-text' %>"><%= x.pct %>%<span><%= fmt(x.projected_days) %> days projected</span></div>
    </div>
  <% }); %>
  <div class="coe-legend">
    <span><i style="background:var(--navy);"></i>Run rate, less the children with finish dates</span>
    <span><i style="background:#4caf7d;"></i>Firm backfill (Offer Accepted / Pre-Offered)</span>
    <span><i class="coe-seg lost" style="width:14px;height:10px;"></i>Days falling away (shown beyond the fill, not inside it)</span>
    <span><i style="background:var(--warn);width:3px;"></i>Placeholder target <%= TGT %>%</span>
  </div>
  <p class="footnote">The track is clipped at 100%: a centre above target fills it and the figure beside the bar carries the real number.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Month by month <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400;font-size:13px;">· projected child-days filled as a share of child-days available</span></h2>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;"><table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Centre</th><th class="num">Places</th><th class="num">Run rate / week</th><th class="num">Leaving by <%= mShort(coe.window.last) %></th>
        <% coe.months.forEach(function(x){ %><th class="num"><%= mShort(x.month) %><br><span style="font-weight:400;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;"><%= x.operating_days %> days</span></th><% }); %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% coe.centres.forEach(function(c){ %>
        <tr>
          <td><a class="row-link" href="/centre/<%= c.owna_id %>"><%= shortName(c.name) %></a><br><span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;"><%= c.enrolled %> enrolled · <%= c.avg_days_per_child.toFixed(1) %> days per child</span></td>
          <td class="num"><%= c.places %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= fmt(c.run_week_days) %></td>
          <td class="num bad-text"><%= c.months[coe.months.length-1].leavers_to_date %></td>
          <% c.months.forEach(function(x){ %><td class="num coe-pct <%= tone(x.pct) %>" title="<%= fmt(x.projected_days) %> of <%= fmt(x.available_days) %> days"><%= x.pct %>%</td><% }); %>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
    <tfoot>
      <tr class="total-row">
        <td>All operating centres</td>
        <td class="num"><%= coe.group.places %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= fmt(coe.group.run_week_days) %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= coe.group.months[coe.months.length-1].leavers_to_date %></td>
        <% coe.group.months.forEach(function(x){ %><td class="num coe-pct <%= tone(x.pct) %>" title="<%= fmt(x.projected_days) %> of <%= fmt(x.available_days) %> days"><%= x.pct %>%</td><% }); %>
      </tr>
    </tfoot>
  </table></div>
  <p class="footnote" style="margin-bottom:0;">Green is at or above the <%= TGT %>% placeholder target, amber within ten points of it, red below. <strong>Leaving by <%= mShort(coe.window.last) %></strong> counts every child whose finish date falls between <%= dLong(coe.as_at) %> and <%= mLong(coe.window.last) %> — the same children are deducted from every later month. The pre-opening centres are not in this table or in the group row: they have no run rate and no licensed places recorded.</p>
</div>

<% if (ms && mm) { %>
<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The measured continuing count <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400;font-size:13px;">· counted from the bookings themselves, not from the run rate</span></h2>
  <p class="sub" style="margin-bottom:14px;">Of the children enrolled today, how many hold bookings that reach into each campaign month. <strong>Continuing</strong> holds at least one booked day in the month. <strong>Not yet confirmed</strong> has none that far out and no finish date — that is the campaign's working list, not a prediction that they leave. <strong>Leaving</strong> has a finish date before the month starts. Counts of children, taken from the snapshot of <%= dLong(ms.snapshot_date) %>.</p>
  <div class="grid kpis" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= fmt(mm.continuing) %></div><div class="l">Children continuing into <%= mLong(am.month) %><span class="cap"><%= mm.continuing_pct %>% of the <%= fmt(mm.enrolled) %> enrolled today<%= mm.centres_beyond ? ' · ' + mm.centres_beyond + ' centre(s) excluded, bookings stop earlier' : '' %></span></div></div>
    <div class="card stat"><div class="n warn-text"><%= fmt(mm.not_confirmed) %></div><div class="l">Not yet confirmed<span class="cap">no bookings recorded that far out and no finish date · worth about <%= fmt(mm.not_confirmed_days) %> child-days at their own booking pattern</span></div></div>
    <div class="card stat"><div class="n bad-text"><%= fmt(mm.leaving) %></div><div class="l">Leaving before <%= mLong(am.month) %><span class="cap">finish date already set in OWNA · <%= fmt(mm.leaving_days) %> child-days at their own pattern, not the centre average</span></div></div>
    <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= fmt(mm.continuing_days) %></div><div class="l">Child-days already booked in <%= mLong(am.month) %><span class="cap">of <%= fmt(mm.available_days) %> available · the run rate projects <%= fmt(ga.projected_days) %></span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;"><table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Centre</th><th class="num">Enrolled now</th>
        <% coe.months.forEach(function(x){ %><th class="num"><%= mShort(x.month) %></th><% }); %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% ms.centres.forEach(function(c){ %>
        <tr>
          <td><a class="row-link" href="/centre/<%= c.owna_id %>"><%= shortName(c.name) %></a><br><span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;"><%= c.avg_days_per_child.toFixed(1) %> days per child per week</span></td>
          <td class="num"><%= fmt(c.enrolled) %></td>
          <% c.months.forEach(function(x){ %>
            <% if (x.beyond_horizon) { %>
              <td class="num muted" title="This centre has no bookings after <%= dLong(c.last_booking_date) %> — not measurable, and not a collapse">—</td>
            <% } else { %>
              <td class="num" title="<%= x.continuing %> continuing · <%= x.not_confirmed %> not yet confirmed · <%= x.leaving %> leaving · <%= fmt(x.continuing_days) %> child-days booked"><strong><%= fmt(x.continuing) %></strong><br><span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;"><%= x.continuing_pct %>%</span></td>
            <% } %>
          <% }); %>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
    <tfoot>
      <tr class="total-row">
        <td>All measured centres</td>
        <td class="num"><%= fmt(ms.months[0] ? ms.months[0].enrolled : 0) %></td>
        <% ms.months.forEach(function(x){ %>
          <td class="num" title="<%= x.continuing %> continuing · <%= x.not_confirmed %> not yet confirmed · <%= x.leaving %> leaving"><strong><%= fmt(x.continuing) %></strong><br><span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;"><%= x.continuing_pct %>%<%= x.centres_beyond ? ' · ' + x.centres_measured + ' of ' + (x.centres_measured + x.centres_beyond) : '' %></span></td>
        <% }); %>
      </tr>
    </tfoot>
  </table></div>
  <% ms.stops.forEach(function(c){ %>
    <p class="footnote" style="border-left:3px solid var(--warn);padding-left:10px;">
      <strong><%= shortName(c.name) %>: its forward bookings stop on <%= dLong(c.last_booking_date) %></strong><%= c.stops_together ? ' — ' + fmt(c.horizon_children) + ' of its ' + fmt(c.enrolled) + ' children have their last booking on that one day' : '' %>. That is how the centre sets recurring bookings in OWNA, not <%= fmt(c.enrolled) %> families leaving: OWNA rolls recurring bookings forward indefinitely for most centres, and a centre that ends them on a fixed date has nothing to count after it. Months past that date are shown as “—”, are left out of the group row, and stay on the run-rate projection until the centre director confirms how the bookings are set (outstanding item 7).
    </p>
  <% }); %>
  <p class="footnote" style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>Enrolled now</strong> is the children with at least one booking in the reference week <%= dLong(ms.centres[0].week.from) %> – <%= dLong(ms.centres[0].week.to) %> — the week with the most children booked in the forward pull, so a holiday week cannot read as a collapse. Public holidays are excluded from every child-day here, as they are everywhere else on this page. <strong>The group row covers only the centres whose bookings reach that month</strong>, so it is not comparable across a month where a centre drops out. Nothing per-child is stored: the snapshot writes counts, and OWNA keeps the records of who the children are.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Booking mix <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400;font-size:13px;">· how many days a week each family is booked, and what that does to days filled</span></h2>
  <p class="sub" style="margin-bottom:14px;">A child on three days a week fills one place but only three fifths of that place's week. This is why places filled and days filled are different numbers, and why the second one is the one the campaign has to move. Measured over <%= dLong(ms.centres[0].week.from) %> – <%= dLong(ms.centres[0].week.to) %>.</p>
  <div class="two-col" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:14px;color:var(--navy);">All operating centres <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400;">· <%= fmt(ms.group.mix_children) %> children, <%= fmt(ms.group.mix_child_days) %> child-days a week</span></h3>
      <% var gmax = Math.max.apply(null, ms.group.mix.map(function(b){ return b.children; }).concat([1])); %>
      <div class="coe-mix">
        <% ms.group.mix.forEach(function(b){ %><div style="height:<%= Math.round(b.children / gmax * 100) %>%;" title="<%= b.children %> children booked <%= b.days_per_week %> day<%= b.days_per_week === 1 ? '' : 's' %> a week"></div><% }); %>
      </div>
      <div class="coe-mix-x">
        <% ms.group.mix.forEach(function(b){ %><span><%= b.days_per_week %> day<%= b.days_per_week === 1 ? '' : 's' %><br><strong><%= fmt(b.children) %></strong></span><% }); %>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:14px;color:var(--navy);">Places filled against days filled</h3>
      <p style="font-size:13px;margin:0 0 8px;"><strong><%= ms.group.places_filled_pct %>%</strong> of the <%= fmt(ms.group.places) %> licensed places are held by a child, but those children book <strong><%= fmt(ms.group.mix_child_days) %></strong> of the <%= fmt(ms.group.places * 5) %> child-days a week those places could carry — <strong class="<%= tone(ms.group.days_filled_pct) + '-text' %>"><%= ms.group.days_filled_pct %>%</strong> of the week.</p>
      <p style="font-size:13px;margin:0;">The group averages <strong><%= ms.group.avg_days_per_child.toFixed(2) %> days per child per week</strong>. Every extra day a week taken by an existing family is worth as much as <%= ms.group.avg_days_per_child >= 1 ? (1 / ms.group.avg_days_per_child).toFixed(2) : '—' %> of a new enrolment, and costs no marketing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;"><table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Centre</th><th class="num">Places</th><th class="num">Children</th>
        <% [1,2,3,4,5].forEach(function(d){ %><th class="num"><%= d %> day<%= d === 1 ? '' : 's' %></th><% }); %>
        <th class="num">Child-days / week</th><th class="num">Avg days</th><th class="num">Places filled</th><th class="num">Days filled</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% ms.centres.forEach(function(c){ %>
        <tr>
          <td><a class="row-link" href="/centre/<%= c.owna_id %>"><%= shortName(c.name) %></a></td>
          <td class="num"><%= fmt(c.places) %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= fmt(c.mix_children) %></td>
          <% [1,2,3,4,5].forEach(function(d){ var b = mixBand(c, d); %><td class="num"><%= fmt(b.children) %><br><span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;"><%= fmt(b.child_days) %> days</span></td><% }); %>
          <td class="num"><strong><%= fmt(c.mix_child_days) %></strong></td>
          <td class="num"><%= c.avg_days_per_child.toFixed(2) %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= c.places_filled_pct %>%</td>
          <td class="num coe-pct <%= tone(c.days_filled_pct) %>"><%= c.days_filled_pct %>%</td>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
    <tfoot>
      <tr class="total-row">
        <td>All operating centres</td>
        <td class="num"><%= fmt(ms.group.places) %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= fmt(ms.group.mix_children) %></td>
        <% ms.group.mix.forEach(function(b){ %><td class="num"><%= fmt(b.children) %><br><span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;"><%= fmt(b.child_days) %> days</span></td><% }); %>
        <td class="num"><%= fmt(ms.group.mix_child_days) %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= ms.group.avg_days_per_child.toFixed(2) %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= ms.group.places_filled_pct %>%</td>
        <td class="num coe-pct <%= tone(ms.group.days_filled_pct) %>"><%= ms.group.days_filled_pct %>%</td>
      </tr>
    </tfoot>
  </table></div>
  <p class="footnote" style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>Days per week</strong> is each child's own distinct booked days in the reference week, so it is what OWNA holds rather than what a family once asked for. A family booked fortnightly counts at the days of that week only. <strong>Places filled</strong> = children ÷ licensed places; <strong>days filled</strong> = child-days a week ÷ (licensed places × 5). Where a centre books above its licensed places, both read over 100% — that is known data problem 2, not a calculation fault.</p>
</div>
<% } else { %>
<div class="card" style="border-left:3px solid var(--muted);">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The measured continuing count and booking mix</h2>
  <p class="sub" style="margin-bottom:0;">Not on this page yet: no snapshot of forward bookings has been taken. The nightly run at 2:15am Sydney takes the first one — or <code>npm run coe-snapshot</code> takes it now — and from then on this page shows, beside the run rate, how many of the children enrolled today hold bookings reaching each campaign month, how many are not yet confirmed, how many are leaving, and how many families are booked 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5 days a week. Everything above works as it does today in the meantime.</p>
</div>
<% } %>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The working, group total by month</h2>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;"><table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Month</th><th class="num">Operating days</th><th class="num">Available</th><th class="num">Run rate</th>
        <th class="num">Leavers</th><th class="num">Leaver days</th><th class="num">Firm starters</th><th class="num">Firm days</th>
        <th class="num">All-pipeline days</th><th class="num">Projected</th><th class="num">% filled</th><th class="num">Gap to <%= TGT %>%</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% coe.group.months.forEach(function(x){ %>
        <tr class="<%= x.month === am.month ? 'coe-anchor' : '' %>">
          <td><%= mLong(x.month) %><%= x.month === am.month ? ' — anchor' : (x.month === '2027-01' ? ' — crossover' : '') %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= x.operating_days %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= fmt(x.available_days) %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= fmt(x.run_rate_days) %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= x.leavers_to_date %><% if (x.leavers_in_month) { %><span class="muted"> (<%= x.leavers_in_month %> this month)</span><% } %></td>
          <td class="num bad-text"><%= sgn(x.leaver_days) %></td>
          <td class="num"><%= x.firm_children %><% if (x.days_unknown) { %><span class="muted"> (<%= x.days_unknown %> est.)</span><% } %></td>
          <td class="num good-text">+<%= fmt(x.firm_days) %></td>
          <td class="num muted"><%= fmt(x.all_days) %></td>
          <td class="num"><strong><%= fmt(x.projected_days) %></strong></td>
          <td class="num coe-pct <%= tone(x.pct) %>"><%= x.pct %>%</td>
          <td class="num"><%= x.gap_days > 0 ? fmt(x.gap_days) : '—' %></td>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="footnote" style="margin-bottom:0;">Every column is child-days unless it says otherwise. <strong>Available</strong> = licensed places × operating days. <strong>Run rate</strong> = the last complete week's booked child-days × (operating days ÷ 5). <strong>Leavers</strong> is a headcount; <strong>leaver days</strong> values them at the centre average from the day after each finish date. <strong>Firm days</strong> counts Offer Accepted and Pre-Offered only; <strong>all-pipeline days</strong> adds every other status (waitlist, tours, new families) and is shown for context — it is <em>not</em> in the projection. <strong>Projected</strong> = run rate − leaver days + firm days. <strong>(n est.)</strong> beside a starter count is how many of those children have no requested days recorded in LineLeader: they are still counted as committed, and their child-days use their centre's mean requested days per week.</p>
</div>

