<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">How every number on this page is calculated</h2>
  <div class="coe-method">
    <p><strong>Child-days available</strong> = licensed places × operating days in the month. Operating days come from the NSW calendar (weekdays, less gazetted public holidays): <%= coe.months.map(function(x){ return mShort(x.month) + ' ' + x.operating_days; }).join(' · ') %>.</p>
    <p><strong>Run rate</strong> = child-days booked in the last complete Mon–Fri week (<%= dLong(coe.run_week.from) %> – <%= dLong(coe.run_week.to) %>), scaled by operating days ÷ 5. It counts every family who has not set a finish date, which is why it is a ceiling.</p>
    <p><strong>Leavers</strong> = children in OWNA with <em>upcoming</em> finish dates on or after <%= dLong(coe.as_at) %>. The headcount is exact. A child counted in one month stays counted in every later month.</p>
    <p><strong>Leaver child-days</strong> = the centre's average booked days per child per week (last complete week ÷ children enrolled) × operating days ÷ 5, prorated by the share of the month falling after the finish date.</p>
    <p><strong>Firm backfill</strong> = LineLeader expected starts at <strong>Offer Accepted</strong> or <strong>Pre-Offered</strong> with a start date on or before the month, valued at the weekdays that family asked for, prorated from the start date. Soft interest is excluded on purpose. Where LineLeader carries no requested days on the enrolment the child is still counted as committed and valued at that centre's mean requested days per week. Starters valued that way are marked <strong>(<%= ga.days_unknown %> est.)</strong> in the tables above — <%= ga.days_unknown %> of the <%= ga.firm_children %> firm starters counted in <%= mLong(am.month) %>. A committed starter is never dropped from the count or from the projection because its days are missing.</p>
    <p><strong>All-pipeline backfill</strong> = the same calculation across every status, including waitlist and tours. It is the secondary figure and never feeds the projection.</p>
    <p><strong>Projected filled</strong> = run rate − leaver child-days + firm backfill, shown as child-days and as a share of available child-days.</p>
    <p><strong>Target <%= TGT %>%</strong> is a <strong>placeholder</strong> only. It should be a per-centre number the CEO sets, and the colours on this page will follow it once it is.</p>
    <p><strong>Why the projection above does not simply add up OWNA's forward bookings:</strong> recurring bookings are rolled forward different distances for each family, so a raw forward month reads as demand when it is really an artefact of how far ahead the roll has run. The run-rate model avoids that. The measured count below it reports the same bookings honestly instead: it says how many children are booked into a month and how many are not yet confirmed, rather than treating the gap as demand that has gone.</p>
    <% if (ms) { %>
    <p><strong>Measured continuing count</strong> = of the children enrolled today at a centre, how many hold at least one booked operating day in the month. <strong>Enrolled today</strong> is the children with a booking in the reference week (the Mon–Fri week with the most children booked in the forward pull, so a holiday week cannot read as a collapse). <strong>Not yet confirmed</strong> holds no booking in that month and has no finish date; <strong>leaving</strong> has a finish date before the month starts. The child-days for those two groups are each child's own days per week scaled to the month's operating days — not the centre average the run-rate model uses.</p>
    <p><strong>Booking mix</strong> = how many children are booked 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5 days a week in that same reference week, and the child-days a week each band represents. It is what separates <em>places filled</em> (children ÷ licensed places) from <em>days filled</em> (child-days a week ÷ places × 5).</p>
    <p><strong>A centre whose forward bookings stop dead on one date</strong> has not lost its families: OWNA rolls recurring bookings indefinitely for most centres, and a centre that ends them on a fixed date (31 December, say) simply has nothing to count past it. Months after that date are shown as “—”, excluded from the group row, and left to the run-rate projection. Outstanding item 7 asks the centre directors which way each centre sets them.</p>
    <p><strong>Stored as counts only.</strong> The nightly snapshot writes numbers — children per month, children per band, child-days — and no name, date of birth or child id, not even a hashed one. OWNA stays the record of who the children are.</p>
    <% } else { %>
    <p><strong>The measured continuing count is pending.</strong> Once the nightly snapshot has run once (2:15am Sydney, or <code>npm run coe-snapshot</code> on demand), this page adds the count of children whose bookings reach each campaign month, the not-yet-confirmed working list, and the booking mix — all counts, no names.</p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="footnote">
  <% if (ms) { %>The run-rate projection above is still a ceiling; the measured continuing count from <%= dLong(ms.snapshot_date) %> is what is actually booked. Per-centre targets from the CEO replace the <%= TGT %>% placeholder.
  <% } else { %>First release: the projection is a ceiling built from the current run rate, not a count of families who have confirmed they are staying. The measured continuing count and booking mix start accumulating from the first nightly run.<% } %>
  <% if (locals.lastRun && lastRun.finished_at) { %>Data as at last sync <%= new Date(lastRun.finished_at).toLocaleString('en-AU') %>.<% } %>
</p>

